    "ra_faqs_fxTqAc": {
      "type": "ra-faqs",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_CmmGpp": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long does the pre-assessment take?",
            "answer": "<p>About two minutes. It contains 10 focused questions designed to identify the most appropriate next step, not reproduce the full assessment.</p>",
            "open_by_default": true
          }
        },
        "faq_tRagy8": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Who should complete it?",
            "answer": "<p>The pre-assessment is intended for people responsible for areas such as supply chain due diligence, procurement, compliance, sustainability, supplier management, risk, or operational oversight.</p><p>You do not need to be a risk specialist to complete it.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_exwbxd": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will I receive a detailed maturity score?",
            "answer": "<p>No. The pre-assessment recommends the most appropriate Level 1, Level 2, or Level 3 assessment pathway.<br/><br/>Detailed maturity scoring, findings, and recommendations come from the full SCDD Maturity Risk Assessment.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_Dz9EYG": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What happens after I submit?",
            "answer": "<p>Your responses are used to recommend the assessment level that best matches your organization’s current position and needs.<br/><br/><strong>If Level 1 is recommended</strong>, you can proceed directly to payment. Once payment is confirmed, our team sends an enrollment key by email so you can start the assessment.<br/><br/><strong>If Level 2 or Level 3 is recommended</strong>, you’ll be directed to schedule a scoping conversation with VECTRA, since these engagements are defined individually.&nbsp;<br/></p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_7EkhRq": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can colleagues help me complete the full assessment?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Once you begin the full assessment, the main respondent can invite colleagues as co-respondents to help answer questions.<br/><br/>Only the main respondent can finalize and submit it — once submitted, the assessment is locked and your reports are generated automatically.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_ChMQAK": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I complete this on behalf of another company, such as a supplier or portfolio company?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Buyers, investors, and private equity firms often purchase the assessment on behalf of the companies they want assessed — for example, a supplier or a portfolio company. In these cases, the paying company and the responding company can be different, and VECTRA coordinates enrollment directly with the company completing the assessment.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_7TNWbF": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is pricing shown immediately?",
            "answer": "<p>Level 2 and Level 3 are scoped individually and route to a consultation with VECTRA, since pricing and required agreements vary by engagement. The final Level 1 pricing and display approach remain subject to approval.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_dzrTfH": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How will my information be used?",
            "answer": "<p>The information you provide is used to process your responses, recommend an assessment pathway, and support any follow-up you request.<br/><br/><a href=\"/pages/privacy-policy\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Privacy Policy\">VECTRA International Privacy Policy.</a></p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_YYitWz": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is a supplier risk assessment the same as a vendor risk assessment?",
            "answer": "<p>The terms are sometimes used interchangeably, but their scope can differ. A vendor risk assessment may cover areas such as technology, cybersecurity, financial exposure, or service continuity.</p><p>VECTRA’s assessment focuses on supplier and supply chain due diligence, including inherent risk, control maturity, and the residual risk that remains.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_nehH6D": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do I need a supplier risk assessment checklist before starting?",
            "answer": "<p>No. You do not need to prepare a supplier risk assessment checklist before completing the pre-assessment. The 10 questions are designed to identify your current position and recommend the appropriate assessment level. Any deeper information or evidence needed will depend on the assessment pathway that follows.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        }
